                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "07f72b77-f4ee-3a80-b4d1-625eaa7f9a54",
                        "entry_id": "10a301e6-384b-3514-8a56-a924dc2160b5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to participate in or incite a revolution or revolt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eadbfee3-3e79-4aba-874a-ae0910719b32",
                                "sense_id": "07f72b77-f4ee-3a80-b4d1-625eaa7f9a54",
                                "text": "The Hawaiians have ‘revoluted’ and dethroned the fat squaw they have hitherto chosen to call a queen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0d58780-7574-450a-866f-79ec08d4700b",
                                "sense_id": "07f72b77-f4ee-3a80-b4d1-625eaa7f9a54",
                                "text": "Christmas always thought himself a “patriotic American,” but, as he saw the matter, a little “revoluting” on behalf of his benefactors—Manuel Bonilla and Estrada Cabrera—in no sense harmed the interestes of the United States."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "77f31f8c-847f-4b25-afa3-6a858c86e397",
                                "sense_id": "07f72b77-f4ee-3a80-b4d1-625eaa7f9a54",
                                "text": "Achimota was Fraser’s life’s work, evidence that ‘the glorious West African people’ were gradually changing their conditions by ‘evolving not revoluting [sic]’."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4626bb5b-63e5-47e6-a726-a9ce9c2eac98",
                                "sense_id": "07f72b77-f4ee-3a80-b4d1-625eaa7f9a54",
                                "text": "2003, Ed McClanahan, Famous People I Have Known\nI rocked and rolled. I ingested illicit substances. I revoluted."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6947468c-438d-44b1-aafb-e35a3d4a1564",
                                "sense_id": "07f72b77-f4ee-3a80-b4d1-625eaa7f9a54",
                                "text": "2004, Samuel Hopkins Adams, The Unspeakable Perk\n“Pins through scarabs,” she laughed, “while beneath you Caracuna riots and revolutes and massacres foreigners."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
